Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Lertaro portable cleanup: removes the two per-user registry entries the running app creates on its
; own (UrlProtocolManager.cs / StartupManager.cs) -- the portable build has no installer/uninstaller to
; do this for you, so run this manually (double-click, confirm the prompt) before deleting the portable
; folder if you want no trace left in the registry. Both are HKCU-only; no elevation is required.
;
; Removes the whole "lertaro://" URI protocol registration (HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Classes\lertaro
; and everything under it, e.g. shell\open\command).
[-HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Classes\lertaro]

; Removes only Lertaro's own "Start with Windows" entry from the shared Run key -- the Run key itself,
; and any other app's entries in it, are left untouched.
[HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Run]
"Lertaro"=-
